263:
The chief of police, or county police officers under the chief's direction, shall:
(1) Execute all lawful orders and directions of the county administrator or board of commissioners;
(2) Maintain the peace, good order and tranquility of the county by the enforcement of all county ordinances and state and federal laws;
(3) Strive to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the police department, and make recommendations from time to time to the board of commissioners for improvements which the board may assist in making in the department;
(4) Make a monthly report in writing to the board of commissioners on the actions of the police department;
(5) Insure that at all times there are sufficient officers on duty to carry out the tasks assigned to the police department;
(6) Discipline officers in accordance with the county personnel policies and procedures;
(7) Maintain written rules and regulations for the police department, approved by the board of commissioners;
(8) Post copies of all police department rules and regulations and this division in a conspicuous place in the department.
(Code 1979, § 2-1-1)

